# Formatter config for the TypeScript surface (task 003). YAML, because a decision this cheap to
# get wrong deserves its reasoning next to it, and JSON has nowhere to put a comment.
#
# Only printWidth departs from prettier's defaults, and it was **measured on this tree**, not
# picked by taste. Reformatting the 31 TS files git holds today costs, per width:
#
#     80 (prettier default) -> 26 files / 1331 changed lines
#     90                    -> 24 files /  754
#    100  <= chosen         -> 15 files /  249
#    110                    -> 19 files /  278
#    120                    -> 22 files /  326
#
# 100 is the minimum of that curve in the band a human would ever pick, and it is where the code
# was already being written by hand. A formatter config that churns the whole tree for no reason
# is a worse trade than one that agrees with what is already there: every line it rewrites is a
# line that no longer says who last changed it for a real reason.
#
# Everything else prettier decides (double quotes, semicolons, trailing commas "all",
# arrowParens "always", 2-space indent) is BOTH the repo's existing style AND prettier's default
# -> deliberately not repeated here. A re-stated default is a second home for a decision that
# already has one, which is the disease CLAUDE.md §4 is about.
printWidth: 100
